WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.610
- All right, we have just
enough time for one more story.

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:03.575
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:03.575 --> 00:00:06.360
(rock music)

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:08.280
Carol Burnett is a living legend.

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:09.480
We saw that all hour.

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:11.640
She's incredibly funny,
but just as important,

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:14.970
she's opened doors for countless
women in entertainment.

00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:15.930
That's not a surprise

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:18.390
according to the founder of Funny Girls.

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:21.180
Funny Girls is a groundbreaking
program under the umbrella

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:23.880
of the Harnisch Foundation
that teaches young girls

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:25.890
leadership skills through comedy.

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:28.080
They say being funny
makes you a better leader.

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:28.913
I agree.

00:00:28.913 --> 00:00:31.530
Here to explain how it works
is the creator of Funny Girls

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:34.800
and executive director for the
Harnisch Foundation, Jenny.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.364
Everybody give it up for Jenny.

00:00:36.364 --> 00:00:37.971
(audience clapping)

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:39.540
What's up, Jenny?

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:41.670
So how does comedy make stronger leaders?

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:42.930
How do you think?

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:45.630
- So, we use improv comedy games

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:48.900
which is making up characters
and plots on the spot

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:51.540
as a fun way to practice
leadership skills.

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:52.740
And it's the training

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:54.810
and practice of those leadership skills

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:58.170
which lets girls know
their voice is important.

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:00.450
They deserve to be seen and heard.

00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:02.250
So that's why we're working with third

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:05.400
to eighth grade girls at
that time when research shows

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.500
that girls start to lose their confidence.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.900
So we're not teaching
the girls to be comedians

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:11.940
like the legendary Carol Burnett.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:13.710
Happy birthday.

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:15.660
Although that would be
amazing if it happened.

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:17.640
But we're teaching them to be leaders,

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:21.720
confident people who aren't
afraid to be seen and heard.

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:22.553
- Absolutely.

00:01:22.553 --> 00:01:24.630
I think it's important too to point out

00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:28.763
that you kinda have them
do silly exercises, right?

00:01:28.763 --> 00:01:29.670
- Yeah.

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:32.640
Some of the exercises are incredibly silly

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:33.990
and funny to watch.

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:35.160
And the first one we try

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:38.940
and you can try this at
home, is Pet Peeve Rant.

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:39.870
You just start ranting

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:41.790
about something that really annoys you,

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:43.920
and you start one at a time

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:45.900
and then everybody adds
their big complaint.

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:48.600
Then we turn it into a
huge chorus of complaining

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:52.320
and it's always super funny
to hear what annoys people,

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:55.700
like singing off-key or
sandwiches cut in the wrong shape.

00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:58.320
We let them go for a minute,

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:00.570
cut them off and say,
"You just did improv."

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:01.403
And they have.

00:02:01.403 --> 00:02:04.170
They came up with their own
material at a moment's notice.

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:07.470
They all succeed because
everybody has a pet peeve

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:09.450
and that game teaches the leadership skill

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:10.470
of self-awareness,

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:13.710
of being able to identify and
express your own emotions.

00:02:13.710 --> 00:02:16.530
So, we're practicing and
learning leadership skills

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:17.781
at the same time that we're laughing

00:02:17.781 --> 00:02:20.790
and having a ton of fun.

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:25.410
- Oh my gosh, I love Pet Peeve Rant.

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:28.020
If I didn't already have
a title for my next album

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:30.055
it would've been called "Pet Peeve Rant."

00:02:30.055 --> 00:02:30.900
(audience laughing)

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:32.050
Would've fit perfectly.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:34.680
Thank you so much, Jenny.

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:36.120
I'm loving what you're doing right now.

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:37.757
I'm liking your post, all right.

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:39.090
(audience clapping)

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:40.050
- [Jenny] Thank you.

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:41.040
- And that's not all.

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:42.750
Our season long partner Pilot Pen,

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:45.360
makers of G2, the go-to pen
of "The Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:46.500
love how Funny Girls

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:49.170
and the Harnisch Foundation
are making a difference.

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:50.010
It's super important.

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:51.450
So they're gonna be writing the foundation

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:52.860
a check for $1,000.

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:53.808
How's that sound?

00:02:53.808 --> 00:02:55.205
(audience clapping)

00:02:55.205 --> 00:02:57.150
- Wow, that's so generous.

00:02:57.150 --> 00:02:58.590
Thank you.

00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:01.290
- Thank you for joining us
and also a big thank you

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:04.500
to Carol Burnett hanging
out with us all hour

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:05.880
and some Colbie Caillat.

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:06.780
Y'all have a great day

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:08.530
and if it's not, try and change it.

